    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and both its tests pass along with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required `contactPreference` = `'EMAIL'` when an email is present, otherwise `'PHONE'`, exposed on the owner response.\n\n`contactPreference` is a pure function of stored owner data, exactly like the existing derived read-only fields `locality` and `initials`. So I followed that established convention rather than inventing a new path:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` string property `contactPreference` to the `Owner` schema. This makes the OpenAPI generator emit `getContactPreference()/setContactPreference()` on the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getContactPreference()` returning `\"EMAIL\"` when `email` is non-blank else `\"PHONE\"`, placed right beside the analogous `getLocality()`. MapStruct's existing `toOwnerDto(owner)` auto-maps it by name \u2014 no mapper, function, or endpoint changes needed.\n\nThe logic lives in one small single-responsibility getter next to its siblings, reuses the existing MapStruct/OpenAPI wiring, and adds nothing to any catch-all class. Both acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full build pass green.",
